<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="Why and What of this page"
	pubDate={new Date('May 23 2026')}
>
  <p>
    I'm Omar, a systems-focused software engineer graduating from Tec de Monterrey.  I am
    deeply driven by technical curiosity, which has led me to dive into distributed
    architectures, functional programming, compiler design, the Linux kernel, and
    low-level engineering.  I like understanding exactly how my tools work under the hood
    and learning from all of them.
  </p>

  <p>
    Beyond my academic coursework, I am the co-founder of <b>Logias</b>, a micro-SaaS
    venture.  Managing our engineering side has given me hands-on experience designing and
    operating multi-tenant cloud infrastructure, optimizing compute and AI costs, and
    deploying highly available services across AWS and Cloudflare ecosystems. As its
    flagship product I recently designed, built, and maintain <b>DataSfera</b>, an
    AI-driven business intelligence engine integrated directly with production enterprise
    ERP systems.
  </p>

  <p>
    On the academic front, I recently completed the Ceneval ISOFT exam (the national
    evaluation for higher education institutions in Mexico), ranking <b>3rd highest in my
    campus batch</b> with an <i>Outstanding</i> designation.  You can view my verified
    results <a href="/ceneval">here</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    I built this website to serve as both a project portfolio and a digital notebook.
    Over the years of experimenting with different technologies, building infrastructure,
    and writing compilers, I've learned a lot of hard lessons. I want to use my blog to
    document these engineering processes and architectural insights, hoping it might be a
    useful resource for others diving into similar domains.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    If you're looking for someone with my profile and experience, or just want to chat
    about tech, feel free to reach out via email at
    <a href="mailto:omar@yoyojambo.com">omar@yoyojambo.com</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    <i>Design Note:</i> This site's aesthetic is heavily inspired by <code>doom-one</code>, my preferred 
    syntax theme from the <a href="https://github.com/doomemacs/themes">Doom Emacs theme megapack</a>. 
    It's built with Astro and raw CSS, focusing on minimal overhead, fast loading times, and clean typography.
  </p>
</Layout>
